frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:2: * Architectural Test: No Command Subclasses
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:4: * This test enforces the architectural principle that Command must NOT be subclassed.
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:5: * Per data-model.md §Command Pattern:
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:6: * - "Architecture: Single Command class (not subclasses) - the real logic is in Operation classes"
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:7: * - "No Subclasses Needed: Tools create operations directly and pass to generic Command"
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:10: * Command is a generic container for Operations. All domain logic belongs in Operation
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:11: * classes (AddFreePoint2DOp, AddLine2DOp, UpdateElementStyleOp, etc.) that implement
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:14: * Having Command subclasses violates the Command/Operation pattern and leads to
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:15: * inconsistent architecture where some logic is in Commands and some in Operations.
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:17: * This test scans the codebase for any `extends Command` patterns and fails if found.
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:20: * Reference: specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/data-model.md §Command Pattern
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:21: * Reference: frontend/src/commands/Command.ts - @sealed documentation
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:28:describe('Architecture: Command Pattern', () => {
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:29:  it('should NOT have any Command subclasses in production code', () => {
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:30:    // Search for "extends Command" pattern in TypeScript files
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:35:      // Use grep to find "extends Command" pattern
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:40:      const command = `cd ${projectRoot} && grep -rn "extends Command" \
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:55:        // Success: No Command subclasses found
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:70:        if (match.includes('"extends Command"') || match.includes("'extends Command'")) {
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:79:          `❌ ARCHITECTURAL VIOLATION: Found Command subclasses in production code!\n\n` +
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:80:          `Per data-model.md §Command Pattern, Command must NOT be subclassed.\n` +
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:85:          `2. Move logic from Command subclass to Operation's apply() and undo() methods\n` +
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:86:          `3. In tool/UI code, create generic Command and add your Operation:\n` +
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:87:          `   const cmd = new Command("My action", world);\n` +
frontend/tests/unit/architecture/noCommandSubclasses.spec.ts:90:          `4. Delete the Command subclass\n\n` +
